#: ../../source/docs/steering-mode.rst:5
#: 51cfb6c21af240d2826b92b44a43aab4
msgid "Steering Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/steering-mode.rst:7
#: f9b2be13f9af4835aa2a5baf4829d3a3
msgid "In Steering mode the user's steering stick controls the vehicle's lateral acceleration and the throttle stick controls the vehicle's speed. At a given steering stick percentage, the vehicle will be controlled to try produce a turn with a lateral acceleration of that percentage of the g-force produced by turning in a  :ref:`TURN_RADIUS <TURN_RADIUS>` turn at the current target speed, not to exceed :ref:`ATC_TURN_MAX_G<ATC_TURN_MAX_G>` G's. So for full stick steering inputs, at lower speeds, the turn radius will be :ref:`TURN_RADIUS <TURN_RADIUS>`, gradually increasing with speed such that :ref:`ATC_TURN_MAX_G<ATC_TURN_MAX_G>` is not exceeded. Once the input returns to neutral, the vehicle will attempt to hold heading, compensating for external influences, ie. \"heading hold\". For ground based vehicles, this attempts to prevent roll-overs or skids."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/steering-mode.rst:10
#: b63b502e50b746e59364530bdd226b9b
msgid "the :ref:`TURN_RADIUS <TURN_RADIUS>` parameter controls the maximum aggressiveness of the turns.  A smaller number results in more aggressive turns.This is the tightest radius that ground vehicles can do, usually at low speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/steering-mode.rst:11
#: a17b278b7ef549abb9aaef85946dde73
msgid "the :ref:`ATC_TURN_MAX_G<ATC_TURN_MAX_G>` parameter sets the maximum limit on lateral G's while steering to prevent roll-overs or skids on ground vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/steering-mode.rst:12
#: a6803622de9e4a4e9260e4f27485f4cc
msgid "when not moving, skid-steering vehicles will pivot in response to steering input but regular steering-throttle rovers will show almost no steering response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/steering-mode.rst:13
#: cfbcb9858e794861bf68a8f89bc3a332
msgid "the top speed is interpolated from the :ref:`CRUISE_THROTTLE <CRUISE_THROTTLE>` and :ref:`CRUISE_SPEED <CRUISE_SPEED>` parameters.  These parameters are described on the :ref:`Tuning Speed and Throttle <rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/steering-mode.rst:14
#: 37f57205f96c4a8b981a85dd6c0530f1
msgid ":ref:`Object Avoidance <rover-object-avoidance>` is active in this mode (if configured)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/steering-mode.rst:15
#: c983c60c741142dcb4f9705910c25e71
msgid "this mode can be used to tune the :ref:`steering rate <rover-tuning-steering-rate>` and :ref:`speed controllers <rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed>` ahead of attempting to tune :ref:`navigation controls <rover-tuning-navigation>`, but using :ref:`Acro Mode<acro-mode>` is preferred to prevent Steering Mode limiting any turn rates."
msgstr ""
